original defects are repaired in these bytes. Delivery causes include verified foreign source fact, incoming ordinal and message digest; distinct deliveries with equal message bytes get distinct seeds, while exact retries retain identity without inserting the creating entry's own hash. Resolved relationship keys are unique per entry, including field/slot/self aliases, with matching receiver and replay checks and both delivery orders. The selected timed input now has a precise exception to its own due-time stop; equal deadlines are ordered, commit rechecks expiry, restart preserves committed drain entries and clock regression does not validate time-sensitive state. Live-item max no longer purports to bound retained final items. Transactional exact counts, complete indexes or scans, incomplete-guard refusal/retry and same-position paged reads preserve absence and count soundness. Numeric retention/work budgets are explicitly R4's unresolved obligation. The three recorded errata now distinguish input-sensitive genesis replay and advisory replay, seed-addressed creation loss, and trusted sender/resolver attempt evidence including missing completions.\n\nRequired corrections (paths and line numbers refer to notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at this exact head):\n\n1. [P2, high confidence] Count failed timed selections in the finite turn budget (429–440, 472–475, 513–527, 1349–1350). The restart count covers stopped commits of the waiting input, and the drain cap covers timed entries actually written. A dropped selected timed commit consumes neither. Concrete permitted clock sequence: previous sealed entry time 3, a live item's deadline 5, each drain selection reads 5, and each selected commit reads 4. The selection is dropped because 4 is before deadline 5, but 4 is not behind the previous entry time 3, so the clock-behind stop does not apply. The drain can repeat forever without a write or a waiting-input commit; both stated counters remain zero. Bound all timed selection/commit attempts or charge their unsuccessful restarts against a finite per-turn budget, including alarm-only turns. Define the unavailable outcome and preserve due work and already committed timed entries. A finite successful-entry cap alone does not make this turn bounded. Include a focused witness for repeated dropped selections and for an alarm-only drain; no execution is requested by this design review.\n\n2. [P2, medium confidence; generic definition contract] Make child-genesis deadline eligibility consistent with activation and replay (311–313, 384–388, 442–453, 556, 795, 1005–1011, 1567–1569). A child genesis names an act kind and the grammar does not expressly exclude an opening timed hold/deadline. The child must write no timed entry until confirmation, yet confirmation is a non-timed delivery and the universal writer/replay rule forbids it ahead of any overdue transition. If a genesis deadline expires while confirmation is delayed, these rules require a timed entry before confirmation and prohibit that entry until after confirmation. The statement that a provisional scope has taken no hold may intend a prohibition, but its validation and replay rule must be explicit. Either exclude timed holds/deadlines from child genesis with matching validation/replay, or state when such deadlines become eligible and the safe confirmation/drain order. Keep any genesis time-relative values' meaning and held-duty dispatch consistent with that order. The issue witness opens no hold; this finding concerns the admitted general definition grammar, not an observed failure of that witness. Add a delayed-confirmation witness or a rejected-definition witness.\n\nNonblocking clarification: 763–784 permits a witness to establish some or count-min from an unfinished scan while also saying an incomplete guard is not judged and final-state guards never pass on partial scans. Define whether a sufficient existential/lower-bound witness is a completed Boolean evaluation even when enumeration is unfinished. Preserve the strict rule that absence, upper bounds and exact counts require complete evidence. This does not reopen the repaired unsafe absence/count finding.\n\nArchitecture: delivery identity and relationship ownership are now coherent across input, wire, fold and recursive foreign replay. The ordered single writer remains the right place for local time, head and guard checks, but the two timer corrections above are needed for bounded progress and an unambiguous activation boundary. R2's exact executable forms and browser states and R3's provisional/founding, current authority, publication and unknown-duty fences remain named dependencies, not approved by this verdict. Retained final-item and guard/read/settlement budgets stay with R4. Full R0–R4 audit/replay, public/manual/browser stories and component retarget/removal remain required.\n\nSecurity: no scope signature or authority is invented from a link, party slot, message digest or transport string. Accepted intent settlement, immutable retained facts, current grant checks and the commit-clock boundary remain intact. Attempt-log claims explicitly rest on complete trusted dispatch coverage and authoritative resolver refusals; replay does not claim independent proof of remote nonexecution. Missing completion or unknown outside effects keep affected correlations, reservations, pins and fences. Unrelated work can proceed. Provisional publication gates preserve held duties, subject to the explicit activation semantics requested above. No live provider security/capacity claim follows from static reading.\n\nSimplification: keep one protocol, one resolved relationship revision number and three typed cause domains. Count aborted timed work within that same protocol rather than adding a second scheduler or authoritative pending-transition table. Clarify provisional eligibility in runtime and replay together. Do not add legacy Artroom formats, adapters, old engines, dual architectures, identity migration maps or prechange replay duties contrary to d4e07064. New-model provenance and unknown external duties are still mandatory.\n\nPreserve the complete commissioned scope and the original builder personal reconciliation obligation; this verdict neither closes that obligation nor substitutes for current owned R2/R3/R4 reviews. The previous causally stale revision4 verdict remains historical; this normal review assesses the actual revision5 artifact subjects independently.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b617518d2d81b05c58578c555f27f5834dca29a","binding":"evidence-only","head":"1ebf4a76e53e85fa9cc0a051add607c94772d982","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f865da9f7d28413a59320f5ba5f953e702f78ec1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f1618167b74b1979e6ccfea174b064caada8999d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}